      "method": null,
      "status": "Reported",
      "calculation_note": "'Typical Properties' table, p.1 (sheet dated 'Revision Date April 2011'). The row label reads '°F, °C' but the pair is printed '-53 (-63)'. Read in label order this would be -53 °F with -63 °C, which do not convert (-53 °F is about -47 °C; -63 °C is about -81 °F). The pair is consistent only as -53 °C (-63 °F): -53 × 1.8 + 32 = -63.4. The other °F, °C rows of this sheet are consistent in label order (Flash Point (COC) 362 (183), Fire Point (COC) 396 (202)). The C12 Dimer column of the Synfluid C12 table DL2-13200.pdf p.1 prints 'Pour Point, °C (°F) -53 (-63)', and the Chevron Phillips 'Synfluid® Dimer C12' data sheet (revision June 2012; copy in reconciliation/audit_evidence) prints 'Pour Point, °C (°F) ASTM D5950 -53 (-63)'. DL2-13202.pdf prints no method, so method is left null.",
      "source": {
        "file": "DL2-13202.pdf",
        "page": 1,
        "revision_date": null
      },
      "notes": "Correction 2026-10-31 (audit CF-136): this field previously stored -63 °C with printed_text '-63', taking the second number of the pair in the row-label order (°F, °C). Corrected to -53 °C on the evidence in calculation_note; the full printed row is quoted in printed_text.",
      "value_final": -53,
      "unit_final": "°C"
    },
